UID:10021757-1786442400-1786449600@events.ubc.ca
SUMMARY:A Foundational Conversation: Anti-Racist Pedagogies in Teaching and Learning
DESCRIPTION:This workshop has been designed for instructors who are interested in joining conversations about anti-racism and looking for an entry point to their learning journey. This session introduces fundamental concepts such as power\, privilege\, and positionality\, as well as the systemic and ideological roots and presentations racialization\, racism\, and racial erasure in the classroom. The session seeks to supports participants as they integrate these fundamental concepts on anti-racism into their teaching and learning practices. \nIntended Learning Outcomes: \n\nReflect on institutional positionality\, power\, and privilege as a faculty\, staff\, or graduate student\nExplore foundational theoretic concepts to anti-racist teaching and learning such as racism\, racialization\, experiences of racial oppression in the classroom and impacts on\nBuild an emerging toolbox of pedagogical and ideological skills to foster a classroom climate rooted in anti-racism\, anti-oppression\, and equity\nReflect on journey to becoming an inclusive educator and ally to racially diverse students and colleagues\n\nPlease register to secure your spot.\nRegister
URL:https://events.ubc.ca/event/a-foundational-conversation-anti-racist-pedagogies-in-teaching-and-learning/
LOCATION:Irving K. Barber Learning Centre\, 1961 East Mall\, Vancouver\, British Columbia\, V6T1Z1\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Audience – Faculty and Staff – Vancouver,Audience – Graduate Students,Subject – Equity, Diversity and Inclusion,Subject – Personal And Professional Development – Faculty,Subject – Personal And Professional Development – Students
ORGANIZER;CN="Centre for Teaching%2C Learning and Technology":MAILTO:ctlt.info@ubc.ca
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
